█▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀█
█ Add Comment                                                                                      █
█ ▎ +Run `viewer FILE`, then press `j` and `k` to move.                                            █
█                                                                                                  █
█  Write   Preview  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── █
█  Mention the arrow keys too.                                                                     █
█                                                                                                  █
█  The README's Keys section should say what this line does in a little more detail. Here's        █
█  what I'd add:                                                                                   █
█                                                                                                  █
█  • j / k move one line and stop at either end of the file; they never wrap around.               █
█  • G jumps to the last line and g to the first.                                                  █
█  • J / K move by hunk, and stop at the first and the last hunk.                                  █
█  • The arrow keys do the same as j and k, and page up and page down move by a screen.            █
█                                                                                                  █
█  I checked each of these against the current build and they all behave as described, so this     █
█  is only a docs change. If you want, I can open a follow-up for wrapping around at the ends,     █
█  but I'd keep it behind a setting so the default stays the same as today.                        █
█                                                                                                  █
█  The help panel lists j as "Line down" but the footer says "Down". We should pick one; I'd go    █
█  with the help panel's wording because it's more specific.                                       █
█                                                                                                  █
█  Steps I ran:                                                                                    █
█                                                                                                  █
█   1. Open a file longer than the screen                                                          █
█   2. Press G                                                                                     █
█   3. Press j, then k, then g                                                                     █
█   4. Press J and K on a file with three hunks                                                    █
█▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄█
